WEBVTT

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.630
Thank you for the encore!

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.840
Did you enjoy the performance?

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.060
Thank you so much for coming!

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.980
On Lancastar?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.530
A 00 concert?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.320
That's the planet you guys came from.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.160
An understudy performance?

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.500
Our own performance?

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.500
No way.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.980
Ready, set, here we go!

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.030
AKB0048!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.900
<i>Lancastar, where our dreams were born.</i>

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.860
<i>Where, without even saying goodbye...</i>

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.070
<i>...we left behind the places we loved.</i>

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.800
<i>Where I left behind Daddy and his objections...</i>

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.490
<i>That Lancastar.</i>

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:06.450
<i>The place where it's all going to start again.</i>

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.500
Allow me to explain the structure of this concert.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.210
This concert is made up of two parts.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.410
The first will be the understudy performance.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.840
The second will be the successors' main performance.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.800
N-N-No way. I can't do it.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.310
I can be on stage... with Youko?

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.360
I'm happy for you, Megu.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.650
The set list will be as follows:

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.680
First, "Shout-out Diamond".

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.790
Second, "Tellin' Myself Maybe".

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.650
Third, "Seaside Cherry".

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.980
They're performing "Seaside Cherry"?

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.830
Yeah.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:54.070
This song has been sung by generation after generation of Center Novae upon their promotions.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.920
It's one of the few solo songs in 00's repertoire.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.260
It must be for Kanata-san or Chieri.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:01.900
Probably.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.880
The one singing it will be Motomiya Nagisa.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.510
Me?!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:11.660
Chieri, Suzuko, and Makoto
will be your backup dancers.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:12.640
Wait a minute!

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.940
I can't do it! Not a solo!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.250
My singing isn't that great. The others—

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.610
This is not up for debate.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.780
I understand.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.200
Aren't you jealous?

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:34.690
Well, I'd be lying if I said I wasn't.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.090
Still, I never managed to get promoted.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.840
Oh, but that doesn't bother me anymore.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:46.080
I guess I'm used to being overtaken by the new girls.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.800
Actually, that's not it.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.250
I know!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:54.190
I'm just glad my teammates are
being rewarded for their efforts.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.140
Yep!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.080
You're one heck of a captain.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.910
Go out there and break a leg!

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:03.500
I'll be watching your back.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.180
Takamina-san, you'll be guarding us?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.570
But, your injuries...

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.440
I'll be up and at 'em by the concert!

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.660
Make sure you do your job as captain for the understudy performance,

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.600
just like the original Takahashi Minami-san would have.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:20.380
Got it!

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:30.050
A concert on Lancastar, huh?

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.560
I hope the ladies from the factory will be there.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.740
Oh, but that would be embarrassing, so maybe not.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.520
Though I guess...

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.820
We've got interstellar mail.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.240
Who's it for?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.870
Let me see.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.940
Oh, they're for me again.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.870
Your parents write to you a lot.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.360
Nah, they're just in it for the gossip.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.960
They ask if Yuuko and Kojiharu get along or if Yukirin goes to the bathroom.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.580
There's another one. Mamoru?

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.540
Oh? The boy you left behind?

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.540
We're just friends!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.680
Let's see here.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.640
"I heard you're holding a concert on Lancastar."

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.270
"But I..."

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.110
Makoto!

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.850
"I don't want you to come back."

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.360
Yuuka...

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.110
Whoops...

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:35.620
<i>The person I most want to come is the least happy about the concert.</i>

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.590
<i>Why am I singing the solo?</i>

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.270
You run past,

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.400
splashing as you go.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.620
I left my sandals...

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:15.990
Wrong!

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.790
"Seaside Cherry" is a <i>vibrant</i> song!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.630
You must capture the tingling sensation of first love!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.340
O-Okay.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:28.110
You're always gazing straight ahead, so you can't tell.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.000
Chieri-san...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.720
While you're singing and doubting yourself,

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.310
the rest of us are dancing.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.930
S-Sorry.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:38.770
Yuuka!

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.260
Why aren't you paying attention?

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.430
You too, Sonata.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.960
This isn't a playground!

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.600
Sonata wasn't playing!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.160
Kanata, you're being too harsh.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.690
We're all doing our best.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.940
Takamina-san and the others are looking out for us.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.940
We can't look lame in front of them.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:55.860
Sickening.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:00.290
All you ever think about is
Takamina-san. It's making me sick.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.390
Yuuka!

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.170
Kanata! Yuuka, you too.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.630
Tsubasa-san!

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.990
Just let it go, Yuuko.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.570
Is it true that S-Quadruple
has composed a new song?

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.350
I heard rumors from the administration.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.810
What's more, I heard that the
song is for the understudies!

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:21.300
Incredible.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:27.310
00 hasn't had a new song since the last
Center Nova, Acchan the 13th, disappeared.

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:34.730
I was going to wait until
after the set list was finalized.

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:38.050
Oh well. Let me announce it now.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:45.250
The encore for the understudy performance will be 00's first new song in a long time.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.960
It is titled "Dreams Are Forever Reborn".

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.180
<i>"Dreams Are Forever..."</i>

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.060
"...Reborn"?

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:01.510
"The stars that shine in the night sky"

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:03.790
"lie billions of lightyears away."

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.290
"Even if the depths of despair"

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:09.320
"should cast an endless shadow,"

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.280
"the truth will make itself heard."

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:16.410
"Who shall be the one to receive"

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.290
"the message of light"

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.550
"set adrift on the river of time?"

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:31.090
Tsubasa-san, why is this song not for us?

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:36.840
This is a song S-Quadruple
composed in response to these girls.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:42.160
S-Quadruple?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:45.060
It is not our place to question his decisions.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:51.980
Furthermore, this shows that these girls had the power to move S-Quadruple.

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:59.440
We're going to practice this song, too.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.150
Yuuko...

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:02.950
We're gonna sing it for the main performance as well!

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:06.960
You're not acting like yourself.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.620
Like myself?

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.740
You mean my usual self?

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:15.380
Or Ooshima Yuuko the 9th?

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.340
Yuuko-san...

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:21.820
Well, it's not like it matters.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.680
Both are the same.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.470
Both are me.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.490
Yuuko!

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:32.770
Yuuko-san!

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:42.700
Why don't we take a break?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.610
But...

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.310
Use this time to let off some steam.

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:55.380
After all, you'll have a big enough challenge to face at the concert.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:05.810
I never knew S-Quadruple was such a big deal.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.870
Indeed.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.140
What a lazybones.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:13.270
He oughta write more new songs.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.980
You're right.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.370
If he did, Yuuko-san wouldn't have acted that way.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.970
I disagree.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:23.420
It'd be a pain to memorize all those new songs.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:28.000
00 already has hundreds of them.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.690
I'd better practice harder.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.950
Don't worry!

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:34.480
Nobody's gonna watch you anyway, Grumbly.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:35.590
What?!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.090
Ow, ow, ow!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.400
It's the Wrath of Grumbly!

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:43.970
Youko!

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:45.470
Megu.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.320
Gimme that!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.560
An indirect kiss for good luck!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.720
Huh?

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:56.520
I'm gonna give it my all.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.990
I'll give a performance that'll put the successors to shame!

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.570
Right...

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.200
Got it.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:15.880
<i>Nagisa must have something that I don't.</i>

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:20.280
<i>That's why I was prepared to accept it.</i>

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:25.890
<i>That song is Nagisa's. I know.</i>

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:29.060
<i>Yet her attitude...</i>

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.310
<i>is unacceptable.</i>

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.560
lie billions of lightyears away.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:52.790
<i>She's a successor, and she even stands in the center position,</i>

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:54.790
People are born, and people die.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.460
<i>yet she's become obsessed over this new song.</i>

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:59.250
Our bodies don't last forever.

00:12:55.990 --> 00:13:02.420
<i>Yuuko-san does not want to hand it over to the understudies.</i>

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:04.930
Those who rise back up from the ashes

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:10.680
give passion to the next generation.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:06.540
<i>It's shameful.</i>

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:12.800
<i>It's so shameful, it's awe-inspiring.</i>

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:20.660
Before we arrive on Lancastar,
there's something you should know.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.570
Lancastar is currently...

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.730
Tsubasa-san.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:25.500
We've received a communication.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.280
Understood. Patch him through.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.270
I'm from the Lancastar
Entertainment Administration.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.790
We appreciate your cooperation.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.880
I'm afraid I have bad news.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:37.340
According to a leak from my department's anti-entertainment faction,

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.880
DES has learned of your planned concert.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:44.630
I'm going to transmit a relatively
secure landing route to you now.

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.810
We shall assist you to the best of our ability.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.240
Thank you very much.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.600
Tsubasa-san?

00:13:57.340 --> 00:14:02.620
Radical anti-entertainment activity is currently taking place on Lancastar.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.600
Anti-entertainment activity?

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.990
Oh no...

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:11.800
But my parents didn't mention anything—

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:17.660
<i>I don't want you to come back.</i>

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:23.320
Nonetheless, we were requested to hold this concert on Lancastar.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:26.880
There are still pro-entertainment officials in the Entertainment Administration.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:32.100
They were the ones who requested this concert.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:37.060
00 once held an entertainment
liberation concert on this planet.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:41.000
They're awaiting the second coming of the miracle

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.300
that moved the hearts of the anti-entertainment faction.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.150
Thank you very much for inviting us.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:57.140
Our pleasure. It's an honor to meet you.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:00.460
We've wagered everything on your concert.

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:01.590
Tsubasa-san!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.500
Please, let us take a look around the town!

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.040
That's too dangerous!

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.140
The area is swarming with DES troops.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:13.080
Right now, your concert is top priority.

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:16.300
We'll make it back in time for the concert.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.680
Please, let us go.

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:21.930
As you wish.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:24.380
However, you will go dressed for battle.

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:27.430
This is no longer the Lancastar you remember.

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.860
Be careful.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.670
Roger!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.830
The smoke is so thick.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:40.330
Statistics say that mining towns
frequently produce 00 members.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.550
So this is where you three grew up?

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:44.490
Yeah.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.660
<i>This hill...</i>

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:50.510
<i>...and this view...</i>

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.760
<i>...haven't changed at all.</i>

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:58.270
<i>Yet, they're somehow tinted
with an unfamiliar foreboding.</i>

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.770
This is the school we used to attend.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:04.700
Huh?

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:07.230
It looks like it's abandoned.

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.360
How come?

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:12.790
It wasn't long ago that we had class here.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.590
Yuuka, is that you?

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:20.950
Mamoru?!

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.080
What are you...

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.140
That uniform...

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:26.420
This is...

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.940
My, is he your friend?

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:30.570
Y-Yes, a friend.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:31.230
Totally.

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:34.380
Y-Yeah...

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.240
Yuuka.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.350
Why did you come back?

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:49.100
Th-That's right! What was the deal with that?

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.040
Why did you tell me not to come?

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:53.060
Well, that's...

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.530
S-Suzuko?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.970
Suzuko?!

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.120
What?!

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.500
This guy's a Suzuko fan.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.840
H-Hey, cut it out!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.300
See?

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.700
What?!

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.770
Thank you for your support.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:22.460
N-Not at all! You're most welcome!

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.930
Hang on. What's the big idea?

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.960
Well, <i>I'm</i> a Yuuka fan.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.970
This guy told me all about you.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.710
My name's Aoi.

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:35.940
Nice to meetcha.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.140
Likewise.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:40.570
Oh man, Yuuka shook my hand!

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:42.560
Jealous, Mamoru?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.230
Why would Yuuka make me jealous?

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:47.420
I've got Suzuko-san.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:50.340
Really, what's so great about Yuuka anyway?

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.540
This is...

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:59.720
Hey, where's your old classroom?

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:01.030
Right here.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.460
It's a mess.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.110
How will they clean this up?

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:12.650
This is something else.

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:16.110
What's goin' on?

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:17.850
I'm tryin' ta sleep here...

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.960
Hey, boys! It's 00!

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.170
Go on.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.130
Make yourselves at home!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.330
Sure...

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:48.440
This school was shut down a few months ago.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:48.830
What?

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:49.650
I don't believe it.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:53.810
It's currently acting as a base for the WOTA Lancastar team.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:55.870
Excuse me...

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.150
Yes?

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.590
May I have a mandarin?

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:06.580
Take as many as you like. They're very sweet.

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.560
Thank you.

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:13.040
You're a piece of work.
What happened to "I hate 00"?

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.130
Well...

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:18.360
After you joined 00, I did some research,

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.430
and the more I learned, the more addicted I became.

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.070
Are you for real?

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:27.480
<i>But it's hard not to feel glad.</i>

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:28.770
No kidding.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.250
Mamoru's always one extreme or the other.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:32.480
That's not true!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.270
Who is this Aoi chick, anyway?

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.240
That's a scary look in your eyes, Yuuka.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.990
I think I'll nickname you Demon.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.920
Sonata!

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:44.320
May I ask something?

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:52.310
K-Kanata-san... I-It's an honor to... to meet you.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:54.960
Chief here is a Kanata-san supporter.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:55.710
Aoi!

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.450
Don't run your mouth!

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:59.000
Come on...

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:02.920
What is the current status of this planet?

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:07.720
Entertainment Liberation

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:07.110
I heard that the Entertainment
Administration was split into two factions.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:07.720
Yes...

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:13.190
The anti-entertainment faction has grown stronger thanks to DES,

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:17.190
and several pro-entertainment officials have been arrested.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:20.900
Is my daddy all right?

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:24.360
Um...

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:27.120
What? What happened? Tell me!

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:32.830
Your father was... arrested.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:40.150
When an Entertainment Administration official's daughter became a 0048 understudy,

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:41.830
it caused problems.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.950
Daddy...

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.540
It's my fault.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:50.560
Wait!

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.010
Where are you going?

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:53.140
But my daddy—

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:54.770
Get down!

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.360
It's DES!

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:02.230
Protect 00! Return fire!

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.360
Roger!

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:07.030
This way. Hurry!

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:09.240
No, we'll help!

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:10.240
Forget that. Just run!

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:11.100
But—

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.420
This isn't the time for that, Yuuka.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:17.170
You need to put on a concert for Lancastar.

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:22.980
Give this planet the courage to fight back.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.170
Please!

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.040
Mamoru...

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:27.890
Understood!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:32.190
Listen up. To confuse the enemy, we'll be leaving in three groups.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.100
Roger!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:44.460
Orine!

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.110
Here it comes!

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.070
It can't be...

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:10.050
Orine!

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:13.330
Orine!

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:24.700
The stars that shine in the night sky

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:24.700
yoru no sora kagayaku hoshi wa

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.280
lie billions of lightyears away.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.280
nanoku kounen no kanata

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:29.820
Even if the depths of despair

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.080
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.820
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.360
should cast an endless shadow,

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.360
mugen no yami to nattemo

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:34.980
the truth will make itself heard.

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:33.280
shinjitsu wa tsutawaru nda

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:34.980
shinjitsu wa tsutawaru nda

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:37.630
Who shall be the one to receive

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:37.630
jikan no kawa ni takushita

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:39.990
the message of light

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:39.990
sono hikari no messeeji

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:42.380
set adrift on the river of time?

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:42.380
uketoru mono wa dare dai?

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:47.510
People are born, and people die.

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:45.340
hito wa umarete hito wa shinde yuku

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:47.510
hito wa umarete hito wa shinde yuku

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:51.980
Our bodies don't last forever.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:47.970
nikutai wa horobiru yo

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:51.980
nikutai wa horobiru yo

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:57.660
Those who rise back up from the ashes

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:57.660
hai no naka kara yomigaeru mono wa

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:03.380
give passion to the next generation.

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:03.380
jounetsu tsugi no sedai e

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.740
Dreams are like reincarnation.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.740
yume wa reincarnation

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:11.680
Like déjà vu, my distant memories

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:11.680
nando demo deja vu no you na

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:13.330
keep coming back to me.

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:13.330
tooi kioku

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:17.530
It's just like reincarnation.

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:17.530
marude reincarnation

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:21.910
With my head still in the clouds,

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:21.910
ima mo mata muishiki no uchi ni

00:23:21.910 --> 00:23:26.090
I'm running off somewhere again.

00:23:21.910 --> 00:23:26.090
dokoka e hashitteru

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:33.110
Will enough tears make me give up?

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:33.110
ikutsume no namida de akirameru no ka?

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:39.150
Will enough lives make my dream come true?

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:39.150
ikutsume no inochi de kanau mono nano ka?

00:23:46.770 --> 00:23:50.580
But I can't bring myself... to hurt it...

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:53.050
I'm going to rescue my father!

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:57.240
I want to help Nagisa—to help our home planet!

00:23:57.240 --> 00:24:01.000
<i>There's no way I'm going to lose just yet!</i>

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:01.000
- Idols Who Sing of Love-
